  "rationale": "**Structural obligations.** The requirement has two:\n1. `Sources` offers `pub async fn search_text(&self, query: &TextQuery) -> Result<TextMatches, SourceError>`.\n2. The source tools expose a `search_text` command.\n\n**Signature.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[search_text]` is declared as `pub async fn search_text(&self, query: &TextQuery) -> Result<TextMatches, SourceError>`. It matches the required signature exactly.\n- It delegates to `self.analysis.provider.search_text(query).await`.\n- `Sources.analysis` is a `SourceAnalysis<LocalSources>`. `impl[LocalSources/SourceProvider]` sets `type Error = SourceError`. The delegated result therefore has type `Result<TextMatches, SourceError>`, with no conversion needed.\n- The provider trait method `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#trait[SourceProvider]/fn[search_text]` has a default body that calls `defaults::search_text`. That helper takes a `&TextQuery` and returns `Result<TextMatches, P::Error>`. It is a trait default reached from the marked `Sources` method, so it needs no separate reference.\n\n**Tool exposure.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<…>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` registers a tool named `search_text`. Its parameters are `pattern` (required), `prefix`, `context_lines` and `limit`.\n- The `dispatch` method in the same impl handles the `\"search_text\"` command. It builds a `TextQuery` and calls `provider.search_text(...)`, so the command is backed by the SDK method.\n\n**Tests.** I checked tests only as context, because this is a structural assessment. Tests marked `{test}` for the search_text behavior and inputs requirements call `search_text` through the tool dispatch. They are in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs`, for example `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results`. Provider-level `search_text` tests are in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs`.\n\nI found no structural gaps and no ambiguity. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments are present or needed.",
